    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by stolen base upside and favorable platoon matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) sits atop the daily efficiency board, benefiting from a prime leadoff spot and a +14% boost from dynamic platoon factors against J. Irvin. His projected 87% success rate against the opposing battery makes him the cornerstone of our SB-focused strategy. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (77.68) and **Yordan Alvarez** (76.93) provide elite anchors; **Junior Caminero** benefits from a +10% park factor, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains a start-of-mind option despite a minor L/L disadvantage, as his xwOBA of 0.465 and favorable wind conditions outweigh the platoon risk. **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Nelson Velazquez** (66.15) also project as strong starts, both capitalizing on a highly favorable matchup against the vulnerable arm of Tomoyuki Sugano and Carson Whisenhunt, respectively.\n\nWhile our starting nine remains high-performing, the bench was a tight consideration. **Carson Benge** (50.14) came closest to cracking the lineup, ultimately squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-efficiency outfielders ahead of him. Despite a respectable +13% boost from the opposing SP skill level, his L/L platoon disadvantage against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez kept him below the threshold required to displace the high-ceiling plays in the current mix. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Gary Sanchez**, **Trea Turner**, and **Chase Meidroth**; their projected scores rely on specific order assumptions that could shift if official lineup cards deviate from our models. Managers should watch for late-breaking weather or lineup changes, particularly for **Trea Turner**, whose value is tightly tethered to his role at the top of the order and the efficiency of his base-running opportunities against the high-delivery-time profile of Andre Pallante.",
